{
 "note": "Design round 9b, feature totem (Where the totem lives), the option chosen: totem-mix. rows are copied from the design's totem-mix.json, verbatim but for one row (each row is the full HUD of build-9b.cjs: hud4.js MIX.render on the situation's state with the fable-boss option, colour style, left-aligned, with the 1.0.0 frame; hotbar slot 5 at cols 36-41 and the offhand at cols 9-14 redrawn by the option, the frame's edges over and under the offhand following its sides). The hearts line is 1.0's: the rows were drawn without the vitals of round 9 (hud.poison draws over t-pop and t-after's skull). situations are the design's inputs: state is the engine's state, ctx.pop the age of the totem's pop in seconds (0: it popped now; 30: it popped 30 s ago and is over; null: no pop), which Hungerbar keeps in its shown-file. Kamal's picks (picks-r9.json picks9b): totem-mix, the mix of the round-9 pick totem-offhand and totem-slot5. The intro and the option's note are reworded where they quoted the design chat as \"Your\" (as the 2026-10-28 renaming did: SOURCES.json renamed). The row of the situation t-out (credits out, the 5-hour used up) is vendored with the 1.1.0 credits-out fix: the design drew 1.0's green offhand sides around the empty well (the engine's paying() lights them while a window is used up, whatever is left), which said \"the credits pay\" when nothing was left to pay with; 1.1.0 draws the frame grey there (src/hud/offhand.ts), so that row's hotbar cols 9 and 14 are the plain grey side (a space on #5D5D5D) and its offhand edges, cols 9-14 of the XP-bar line and of the bottom edge row, the frame grey, and nothing else in it changed.",
