 "id": "totem-mix",
 "name": "In the hotbar, swapped to the offhand when needed",
 "optionNote": "The idea from the design chat. While nothing is low the totem waits in hotbar slot 5 (gold ☥, no count), and the emerald keeps the offhand and its dollars. When a window drops to 10% left or less, the totem swaps into the offhand: slot 5 empties and the offhand shows ☥ with your dollars, exactly as \"Totem in the offhand\" draws it. At 0 it pops there for 30 seconds (☥✦ between gold sides), then the green paying emerald. With the credits out, or no extra usage, there is no totem anywhere. So the totem is always visible while you hold one, and its move to the offhand is the warning.",
 "title": "Where the totem lives",
 "intro": "The note on the totem from the design chat: \"mixing both Totem in the offhand and Totem in hotbar slot 5 so it in hotbar and when needed to use it switch and goes to the offhand\". That is how Minecraft players carry a Totem of Undying: one in the hotbar, swapped into the offhand when a fight turns bad. Slot 5 is free now (the allays took the agents' job), so the totem can wait there. The week is at 60% in every situation below, so only the 5-hour window moves the totem.",
